Yes. I would make the PaymentProvider service the core integration boundary of the Chama system.

One important correction to the earlier idea: we should not pretend that one provider gives unrestricted access to every Kenyan bank account. The providers expose different capabilities. For example, KCB BUNI currently advertises payments across all banks and mobile-money networks, while its account-information APIs are for KCB-connected banking information. Jenga documents broader payment services but currently documents its Account Services around Equity. NCBA offers its own API/host-to-host and collection/reconciliation solutions. 

